# Copy to .env.local to point a local checkout at a real Supabase project.
# Leave it alone and `npm run dev` runs on seed data with the stubbed sign-in —
# which is the point: nobody needs a secret to work on a screen.
#
# On Netlify these two live in Site configuration → Environment variables.
# The anon key is public by design: the tables are protected by the policies in
# supabase/migrations/0002_rls.sql, not by keeping that string quiet. The
# service_role key is a different thing entirely and belongs nowhere near here.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...
